so I switched to try_files, and it is returning index.html for the favicon.  I looked through the docs and wasn't able to find where {path} comes from or if there are other similar ones, because I think what I want would be closer to try_files {path} {filename}

```
:80 {
	root * /files
	log

	try_files {path} /index.html
	file_server

}
```

Going only by your description of "without an extension" and "with a file extension", this works:

```caddyfile

example.com {
	log
	@participant4 `path_regexp('/[^.]+$')`
	handle @participant4 {
		try_files {path}/index.html index.html
	}
	@participant5 `path('*.*')`
	handle @participant5 {
		try_files {path} {file} =404
	}
	file_server
}

```

